method. Thus, it was made a private member of the dArray class while quickSort was
made public. The int variables in swap designate the elements that are to be swapped in
the dArray object while the left and right arguments for quickSort specify the index
subrange on which the algorithm will be applied.
The definition of the swap method is
dArray :: swap ( i , j ){
temp = pA [ i ]; pA [ i ] = pA [ j ]; pA [ j ] = temp ;
}
Temporary storage is used to hold the value of one array element while it is overwritten
after which the remaining component is replaced with the stored value. The implementation
of the quicksort algorithm then takes the form
dArray :: quickSort ( left , right ){
pivotIndex = floor (( left + right ) 2);
pivot = pA [ pivotIndex ];
low = left , high = right ;
( high >= low ){
( pivot > pA [ low ])
low ++;
( pA [ high ] > pivot )
high - -;
( low <= high ){
swap ( low , high );
low ++; high - -;
}
}
( left < low - 1)
quickSort ( left , low - 1);
( low < right )
quickSort ( low , right );
}
