The C++ floor function (along with a cast) is used here to transform double precision keys
into integers. Although e ff ective, this is not the best solution to the problem; a generic class
should not really need adjustments to allow for di ff erent types of data. A more satisfactory
solution is to overload the modulus operator for the Key class in a way that gives the desired
result in the form of a generic hash function in the chainHash class. This approach will be
examined in Exercise 10.21.
